  "paragraph": 13,
  "text": "You see the same principle in how coding harnesses edit files. Early agents asked the model to rewrite an entire eight-hundred-line source file from top to bottom just to fix a five-line race condition. That wastes output tokens, burns seconds of latency, and invites accidental deletions. Modern harnesses like Aider, Claude Code, and Cursor pair line-numbered file reads with targeted search-and-replace or diff-merge edits, cutting output tokens by an order of magnitude while making every change fast and easy to verify.",
